  "mechanismSummary": "Tosylation makes a leaving group without touching the carbon: the alcohol oxygen attacks sulfur, chloride leaves, and pyridine removes the proton. The C–O bond survives, so the configuration at carbon is kept: (R)-butan-2-ol gives the (R)-tosylate. The tosylate can then be displaced by SN2, with inversion.",
